In the {{ill|Na Jia|ja|納甲|12=draft}} system, Li is associated with {{ill|Ji (己)|ja|己|1=Tsuchinoto (己)|12=draft}}, the Earth element in {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=Wuxing|ja|五行思想|12=draft}}, and the center among the {{ill|Five Directions|ja|五方|12=draft}}.
== Earlier Heaven Arrangement == In the {{ill|Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|ja|伏羲先天八卦|12=draft}}, Li is the third in sequence and is positioned as one of the four cardinal trigrams, representing the {{ill|east|ja|東|12=draft}}. In terms of Yin-Yang transformation, it has two Yang lines and follows the {{ill|Zhen|ja|震|1=Zhen (Bagua)|lt=Zhen|lt=Zhen (☳)|12=draft}} trigram.
