== Trigram Symbolism == The outer part of the trigram is Yang and strong, while the inner part is Yin and gentle. The original meaning is "outwardly bright but dark within." It also represents "two things facing each other with one in between." Li symbolizes {{ill|fire|ja|火|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|light|ja|光|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|lightning|ja|稲妻|12=draft|12=draft}} (the light of {{ill|thunder|ja|雷|12=draft|12=draft}}), beauty, {{ill|pheasants|ja|雉|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|eyes|ja|目|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|the heart|ja|心臓|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|breasts|ja|乳房|12=draft|12=draft}}, joy, splendor, middle-aged women, separation and opposition, conflict, appearance, and the colors red or purple. As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|12=draft|12=draft}}, it represents the {{ill|south|ja|南|12=draft|12=draft}}<ref>「[https://www.ndl.go.jp/koyomi/chapter3/s2.html 干支2方位神]」National Diet Library, accessed December 16, 2021.</ref> and corresponds to {{ill|Wu (午)|ja|午|1=Horse (zodiac)|lt=Horse (午)|12=draft|12=draft}} in the {{ill|Earthly Branches|ja|地支|12=draft|12=draft}}.
In the {{ill|Na Jia|ja|納甲|12=draft|12=draft}} system, Li is associated with {{ill|Ji (己)|ja|己|1=Tsuchinoto (己)|12=draft|12=draft}}, the Earth element in {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=Wuxing|ja|五行思想|12=draft|12=draft}}, and the center among the {{ill|Five Directions|ja|五方|12=draft|12=draft}}.
== Earlier Heaven Arrangement == In the {{ill|Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|ja|伏羲先天八卦|12=draft|12=draft}}, Li is the third in sequence and is positioned as one of the four cardinal trigrams, representing the {{ill|east|ja|東|12=draft|12=draft}}. In terms of Yin-Yang transformation, it has two Yang lines and follows the {{ill|Zhen|ja|震|1=Zhen (Bagua)|lt=Zhen|lt=Zhen (☳)|12=draft|12=draft}} trigram.
