[[sn:Li (Bagua)]] [[ja:離]] [[ja:九星]] [[ja:魔方陣]] [[ja:後天定位盤]] [[ja:五行思想]] [[ja:木]] [[ja:火]] [[ja:土]] [[ja:金]] [[ja:水]] [[ja:十干]] [[ja:十二支]] [[ja:八卦]] [[ja:易経]] [[ja:禹]] [[ja:夏王朝]] [[ja:洛水]] [[ja:洛書]] [[ja:河図洛書]] [[ja:陰陽道]] [[ja:方位]] [[ja:運勢]] [[ja:吉凶]] [[ja:一白水星]] [[ja:北]] [[ja:坎]] [[ja:二黒土星]] [[ja:坤]] [[ja:三碧木星]] [[ja:東]] [[ja:震]] [[ja:四緑木星]] [[ja:巽]] [[ja:五黄土星]] [[ja:太極]] [[ja:六白金星]] [[ja:乾]] [[ja:七赤金星]] [[ja:西]] [[ja:兌]] [[ja:八白土星]] [[ja:艮]] [[ja:九紫火星]] [[ja:南]] [[ja:太陽系]] [[ja:相性]] [[ja:吉方位]] [[ja:易]] [[ja:高島易断]] [[ja:風水]] [[ja:気学]] [[ja:陰陽五行説]] [[ja:暦注]] [[en:draft:Li (Bagua)]] [[sn:Li]] [[ko:%EC%9D%B4 (%EA%B4%98)]] [[pt:L%C3%AD (I Ching)]] [[nl:Vuur (trigram)]] [[fr:L%C3%AD]] [[sn:i]] [[en:Li]] [[ar:Li (Bagua)]]

{{Bagua|qq=}} '''Li''' (離) is one of the {{ill|Bagua|ja|八卦|qq=|12=draft}}. Its trigram form is {{resize|125%|'''☲'''|qq=}} with the first {{ill|Yao (lines)|ja|爻|qq=|12=draft}} being Yang (⚊), the second being Yin (⚋), and the third being Yang (⚊). It is also one of the {{ill|Sixty-Four Hexagrams|ja|六十四卦|qq=|12=draft}}, known as {{ill|Li as Fire|ja|離|1=Li (Bagua)|lt=Li為火|qq=|12=draft}}, consisting of Li below and Li above.
== Trigram Symbolism == The outer part of the trigram is Yang and strong, while the inner part is Yin and gentle. The original meaning is "outwardly bright but dark within." It also represents "two things facing each other with one in between." Li symbolizes {{ill|fire|ja|火|qq=|12=draft}}, {{ill|light|ja|光|qq=|12=draft}}, {{ill|lightning|ja|稲妻|qq=|12=draft}} (the light of {{ill|thunder|ja|雷|qq=|12=draft}}), beauty, {{ill|pheasants|ja|雉|qq=|12=draft}}, {{ill|eyes|ja|目|qq=|12=draft}}, {{ill|the heart|ja|心臓|qq=|12=draft}}, {{ill|breasts|ja|乳房|qq=|12=draft}}, joy, splendor, middle-aged women, separation and opposition, conflict, appearance, and the colors red or purple. As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|qq=|12=draft}}, it represents the {{ill|south|ja|南|qq=|12=draft}}<ref>「[https://www.ndl.go.jp/koyomi/chapter3/s2.html 干支2方位神]」National Diet Library, accessed December 16, 2021.</ref> and corresponds to {{ill|Wu (午)|ja|午|1=Horse (zodiac)|lt=Horse (午)|qq=|12=draft}} in the {{ill|Earthly Branches|ja|地支|qq=|12=draft}}.
In the {{ill|Na Jia|ja|納甲|qq=|12=draft}} system, Li is associated with {{ill|Ji (己)|ja|己|1=Tsuchinoto (己)|qq=|12=draft}}, the Earth element in {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=Wuxing|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|qq=|12=draft}}, and the center among the {{ill|Five Directions|ja|五方|qq=|12=draft}}.
== Earlier Heaven Arrangement == In the {{ill|Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|ja|伏羲先天八卦|qq=|12=draft}}, Li is the third in sequence and is positioned as one of the four cardinal trigrams, representing the {{ill|east|ja|東|qq=|12=draft}}. In terms of Yin-Yang transformation, it has two Yang lines and follows the {{ill|Zhen|ja|震|1=Zhen (Bagua)|lt=Zhen|lt=Zhen (☳)|qq=|12=draft}} trigram.
